-- title:
--   A finite spanning order for the two prolongations at level Nq
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $N\ge 1$, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ a ring homomorphism; let `data` be modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, let the degeneracy inclusions `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` from level $N$ to level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be integral (hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$), let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data and $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$. Assume $q\nmid N$ and $\mathrm{red}$ surjective. Write $V$ for the subring of the level-$N$ field $\overline{F}_N=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` consisting of elements whose Laurent series lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized N A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with $j(\mathfrak q)$ and $j(\mathfrak q^N)$ at the prime of elements killed by reduction; make $\overline{F}_{Nq}$ a $V$-algebra along the inclusion `heckeAlphaBar`. Then there is a $V$-subalgebra $S$ of $\overline{F}_{Nq}$ such that: (1) $g\in S$ exactly when the Laurent series of $g$ and of $w_q g=$ `atkinLehnerBar N q g` both lie in `modularLocalized (N*q) A.toSubring red`; (2) `heckeAlphaBar` carries every $v\in\overline F_N$ with Laurent series in `modularLocalized N A.toSubring red` into $S$; (3) `jQFun N q`, the element with $\mathfrak q$-expansion $j(\mathfrak q^{q})$, lies in $S$; (4) the element with $\mathfrak q$-expansion $j(\mathfrak q^{Nq})$ lies in $S$; (5) $S$ is a finite $V$-module; (6) $S$ spans $\overline F_{Nq}$ over $\overline F_N$ along `heckeAlphaBar`; (7) for every pair $a,b$ in the level-$N$ function field `modularFunctionFieldC k N` over $k$ there is $s\in S$ with both $s$ and $w_q s$ localised at level $Nq$ whose reductions under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom (N*q)` are $a$ and $b$; (8) the reductions at levels $Nq$ and $N$ agree on any Laurent series localised at both levels; and (9) for $v\in\overline F_N$ localised at level $N$, the level-$Nq$ reduction of $w_q(\mathrm{heckeAlphaBar}\,v)$ is `qExpand k q` applied to the level-$N$ reduction of $v$.
--
--   This produces the ring of common integers of the two prolongations of the level-$Nq$ function field at a place above $q$ — the order over the localised level-$N$ ring whose reduction realises the two components of the Deligne–Rapoport special fibre of $X_0(Nq)$, the second component being reached through the Atkin–Lehner transport and the $q$-power substitution on $\mathfrak q$-expansions. It is used in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.normReduction_of_not_dvd_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.normReduction_of_not_dvd_of_surjective).
